<div class="container mx-auto">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap">
    <div class="flex-grow w-full">
      <div class="text-center mt-sm-5 px-12">
        {# Spinner styles are hardcoded in 00-head.twig #}
        <div class="spinner">
          <div class="double-bounce1"></div>
          <div class="double-bounce2"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex justify-center">
          {% set welcome_image = {
            variant: 'primary',
            src: paths.images ~ '/utc-horizontal-logo.png',
            alt: 'University of Tennessee Chattanooga'
          } %}

          {% include '@atoms/image/_image.twig' with {
            image: welcome_image
          } %}
        </div>

        <h1 class="mt-12 text-3xl">
          Welcome to The University of Tennessee Chattanooga's Atomic Design System
        </h1>
        
        <p class="mt-12 text-left">
          UTC uses the Particle theme, a Drupal starterkit, to help developers implement UTC's branded design system with Webpack and Twig. TailwindCSS has been custom added for your convenience.
        </p>

        <p class="text-left">
          Start exploring by clicking the Atomic Design links in the menu. For vastly more information about
          how to use Particle, <a href="https://phase2.gitbook.io/frontend/particle/intro" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> check out the docs</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-left">
          For more information about Atomic Design principles, please visit author, Brad Frost's, article, "<a href="https://bradfrost.com/blog/post/atomic-web-design/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">atomic design</a>".
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
